            "text": "Piping a remote download into a shell — `curl ... | sh` is dangerous: the remote script can change at any time, MITM can swap the payload, and the build is not reproducible. There's also no signature check."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "file:///C:/Users/nacho/Documents/GitHub/Docker-Hardening-Checker/samples/Dockerfile.bad",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 12
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "high",
            "remediation": "Download to a file, verify its checksum or signature, then run.",
            "snippet": "RUN curl -sSL https://get.example.com | sh"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DF-009",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Sensitive port EXPOSEd: 22 — Port 22 is a well-known management port (SSH, RDP, Postgres, etc.). Exposing it inside an image is a strong smell — the application should not expose management interfaces at all."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "file:///C:/Users/nacho/Documents/GitHub/Docker-Hardening-Checker/samples/Dockerfile.bad",
